    "title": "Valid Anagram",
    "workload": "build 8 string pairs of 20000 lowercase chars once (t is s reversed, so an anagram; odd-indexed pairs shift one character to break the multiset without changing the length), then 8000 punches of the 26-slot frequency pass. The counting loop has no early exit, so true and false cases do identical work and only the final 26-slot check differs. Sink weights successes by iteration. NOTE: every language runs the same fixed 26-slot array here -- no data-structure divergence to caveat.",
